{
  "id" : "starforge-imperviumorigins",
  "species" : "glitch",
  "title" : "The Origins of Impervium",
  "description" : "A short history of the galaxy's toughest alloy.",
  "icon" : "starforge-glitchkatahelcover3.png",
  "contentPages" : [

"Impervium was first discovered by Avian Stargazers around three centuries ago. It is, by far, the strongest alloy we currently have access to, surpassing Solarium-infused Violium by quite a margin. To this day, we've found so little of it that we're still unsure how exactly it's created. It is theorized that it forms when a meteor containing various, unknown metals flies close to a powerful sun, causing them to melt and fuse together, creating our alloy - named Impervium after its incredibly impervious nature.",
"Now, my lord Katahel got his hands on a rare sample, just enough to make the tip of a spear or a crossbow bolt. He tasked me with finding more and giving him the means to rule eternally, a body of Impervium, one that will not melt, rust or age. But how? How do I get my hands on something so incredibly rare and expensive?
Well the answer was just below my feet. Well, below Katahel's castle to be precise. The incredible ^magenta;Starforge^reset;.",
"It took me ages, but after a ton of research I figured out how it works. It's basically like a pixel printer, but with Ancient Essence! Obviously, it's a lot more complex than that, but with a base blueprint and the component's parameters, it's possible to create an almost exact copy using the Essence and various raw materials! After various trials and errors, I made it! Starforged Impervium! Our synthetic version, while much cheaper, still used up the majority of the Castle's Essence.",
"This Impervium was used to arm Katahel's High Knights. Impervium shields, highbrands, broadswords, you name it. I even had enough to make my lord Katahel a whole suit of heavy armor. I'm confident it was the toughest armor any Glitch has ever worn. I needed more time to figure out if an Impervium body was even possible... I needed to experiment with this ^magenta;Starforge^reset; a little more. That's how I came to create the Roboblins, Robogres and so much more... But that's a story for another day." 

  ],
